| 140 | the library's `strToFloat` mis-parses a sign and overflows on a long mantissa under walk (the compiled prelude has no `strToFloat`): `strToFloat "-1.5"` is `-28.5`, and a 17-digit mantissa dies with `Overflow of ZZ32 100000000000000000` | NEGATIVE-VERIFIED | library bug (library) | silent | none | run-c | `strToFloat` (`Library/FortressLibrary.fss:4606-4611` at c124c6b65, "Quick and dirty implementation") sums `10^k (both[\|both\| - 1 - k].codePoint - '0'.codePoint)` under `SUM[\ZZ32\]` over every character, sign included, so `-` counts as -3 and `"-1.5"` is (-3*100 + 1*10 + 5)/10 = -28.5; and `10^k` is a `ZZ32`, which overflows at the 10th digit; `"1.5"` parses right. Workaround: `parseFloat` in `explorations/run-c/src/FlatData.fss:13` (digits into an `RR64` mantissa, a power of ten, `-` and the high minus, an `e`/`E` exponent). Probe `explorations/run-c/probes/g140_strtofloat.fss`, in the parent of 4ebf80aec; full text: history, row 140 |
